{"author":{"id":"694fb8161bd8bf91df2a28db7c649e48f8c5fa47ad3ad0234607d35f0482801a"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790280535,"nonce":"/YfzqdCzqqnd3RrSfBklKAiQHhQ=","title":"Windows: wlift --aot to .exe, guard pages on krio stacks, aarch64","message":"Split from 6389b29, whose runtime work on windows-2022 is done. What\nthe Windows target still lacks:\n\n- AOT linking. link_executable in src/codegen/aot.rs branches on\n  macOS and Linux only and drives cc with -o, -lpthread, -ldl, -lm, so\n  `wlift --aot` on Windows has no linker path. The site's Windows page\n  promises an .exe. Needs an MSVC branch (link.exe or cl, /OUT:, the\n  system libraries the staticlib pulls in: ws2_32, userenv, ntdll,\n  bcrypt, advapi32, and the stack reserve the other branches set with\n  /STACK) and an AOT job on windows-2022 to prove it.\n- Guard pages on krio stacks. Fiber stacks on Windows are heap\n  allocations with nothing below them, so an overflow writes into\n  whatever the allocator placed there instead of faulting.\n- aarch64-pc-windows is not claimed: krio does not switch stacks there.","files":null}]}